<p>A magnitude 5.8-5.9 earthquake struck Afghanistan on Friday, and authorities said at least eight people were killed and a child was injured after a house collapsed on the outskirts of Kabul. The quake&#x27;s epicenter was in Afghanistan, but tremors spread across parts of Pakistan and northern India, including Islamabad and New Delhi. Officials were still assessing the full extent of the damage, and reports from remote areas near the quake zone may take time to come in. Even so, the quake was another reminder of how exposed the region remains to seismic shocks, as authorities worked to gather damage reports and monitor affected communities across borders.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/8aU6mG-DCgMKneMxEPdqbRSJRYU8VHvfVC1CqK9ikM_yZOfXqxPOh30p_BU7B2IiFxKFFmCMLeDyTNwcVKe4lqxYNgC7cWepnLDoW6XXvRe1SoBKv078uzfRMjGny2cdktfKpb-bkqa9R1PchdRCGAjZGlalGLvkUxMg_pqjcO406UBQr_fJL7tyrx_tSpAqNl6iitPdLGg5WC7okMqvdcrB70tD7z4MTK9HTR5bTYwTrNhiXpibjoiVmtdWaehAGz92NAnJ8a_o68Ik1g' alt='FILE PHOTO: Afghan women in burqa walk towards a safer place after their house was damaged following a deadly magnitude 6 earthquake that struck Afghanistan on Sunday, at Lulam village, in Nurgal district, Kunar province, Afghanistan, September 3, 2025. REUTERS/Sayed Hassib/File Photo/File Photo' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Deep epicenter: The quake struck at a depth of about 150 kilometers, which helped tremors travel widely into Pakistan and northern India.</li><li>Cross-border tremors: People felt the shaking in cities including Islamabad and New Delhi, underscoring the earthquake&#x27;s reach beyond Afghanistan.</li><li>Assessment delays: Authorities warned that damage estimates could take time because the quake&#x27;s center was in a remote area.</li><li>Recent pattern: Coverage noted that earthquakes in this region have killed thousands of people in recent years, underscoring its recurring seismic risk.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Afghanistan National Disaster Management Authority: The agency said eight people were killed and one child was injured when a house collapsed in Kabul after the quake. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/8-dead-after-earthquake-of-magnitude-5-9-strikes-afghanistan-11308969#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>German broadcaster DW, citing officials: Officials said they were still assessing the overall damage and that reports could be delayed because the quake&#x27;s center was in a remote area. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-earthquake-of-magnitude-5-9-kills-at-least-8/a-76657899'>DW</a>)</li><li>Indian media and observers: Reports in India emphasized that tremors were felt across several northern areas, showing that the quake&#x27;s effects reached well beyond the epicenter. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/earthquake-today-3-april-2026-afghanistan-epicentre-tremors-delhi-jammu-pakistan/article70821067.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/8-dead-after-earthquake-of-magnitude-5-9-strikes-afghanistan-11308969#publisher=newsstand'>8 Dead After Earthquake Of Magnitude 5.9 Strikes Afghanistan</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-earthquake-of-magnitude-5-9-kills-at-least-8/a-76657899'>Afghanistan earthquake of magnitude 5.9 kills at least 8</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/58-magnitude-quake-hits-afghanistan-pakistan-killing-8-131695467'>5.8 magnitude quake hits Afghanistan and Pakistan, killing 8 in Afghanistan</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/earthquake-today-3-april-2026-afghanistan-epicentre-tremors-delhi-jammu-pakistan/article70821067.ece'>Earthquake tremors felt in several parts of north India</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-58-magnitude-quake-hits-afghanistan-and-pakistan-killing-eight/'>5.8 magnitude quake hits Afghanistan and Pakistan, killing eight</a